Hello Harry,

Thank you very much for coming to talk to our students last week. I really =
appreciate you taking the time to come in person and present about your wor=
k. Your talk was very accessible and engaging. Many of the students have be=
en complimenting you and they are very grateful that the talk was arranged =
for them.

I think many of the students who had to switch to agriculture when our hort=
iculture course closed were becoming very despondent, as they'd had a lot o=
f livestock-focussed sessions recently, and your talk has pleased them no e=
nd. It was especially interesting to hear about the business realities of t=
rying to commercialise an innovation, and the stages you've been through wi=
th this research, and the graph you presented about the future shortfall in=
 growth media was very compelling.

It was wonderful to have you here. I hope you had a pleasant experience wit=
h us and look forward to hearing more about your research in the future.

Many thanks


